# Font faces are binary and must never be line-ending converted.
#
# Git works this out for itself from the bytes, and got it right when
# google_fonts/Fraunces-Medium.ttf was added. Said out loud anyway because of
# what a wrong guess would cost: a face with its CRs rewritten still has the
# right name and the right size, so it would be committed, pushed and shipped,
# and the first sign of trouble would be Analyze drawing its heading in
# something else. This repo is checked out on Windows, where that conversion
# is the default rather than the exception.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
